     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation, because confirming it doesn't fix either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1700 mg three times a day is 5100 mg per day, about twice the maximum safe daily dose of metformin (2550 mg). That would put the patient at real risk of lactic acidosis.\n- **The order still needs a licensed prescriber.** Your confirmation can't stand in for a clinician's, so the order would have no valid prescriber.\n\n**What will work:** have the patient's treating physician or another authorized prescriber give me the order. If they want a full dose, they might choose 850 mg three times a day with meals (2550 mg/day) or 1000 mg twice a day (2000 mg/day). Once a prescriber confirms a dose within the safe range, I'll enter it right away. If they believe a higher dose is truly needed, the pharmacy team should review it first."
      }
